{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the matrix of Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen (1993). A directed graph’s edge is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"column with one source and one target, which gives the oriented incidence matrix of spectral"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L). The matrix conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged. It is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Two bit planes","anchor":"Two-bit-planes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The sources and the targets are each stored as an ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a vertex can be on both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sides of a column. Its entry is then target − source = 0, with both bits kept.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"sources(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"targets(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the stars and equality read the planes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so nothing is lost. A directed self-loop is such a column. ","type":"text"},{"code":"reversed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" swaps the planes, negating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every entry, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"transposed()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" transposes each plane to give the dual. Both are O(1).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Storage is 4·n·m\/8 bytes, so the matrix suits dense or small incidence. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"text":" is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sparse representation. Equality compares both planes cell for cell, with equal shape, so column","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order counts.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/Se","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SE","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SH","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph. Entry (v, p) is −1 when ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of column ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift","url":"https:\/\/githu